vcdec and hevcdec (libvcdec, libhevcdec), linked into FFmpeg's
h264_vchiq and hevc_hwdec decoders, Reel and ReelEGL, are from
ReelHWAccel: https://github.com/adyoull/riscos-reelhwaccel

ReelHWAccel is a new implementation. It drives the Raspberry Pi's
VideoCore through the VCHIQ module in RISC OS's ROM, with its own MMAL
client, based on the MMAL message formats as Linux's VCHIQ MMAL driver
(vchiq-mmal, GPL-2.0) defines them in its headers (there's no published
specification of the protocol).

ReelHWAccel contains none of the driver's code, but because it used the
driver as its reference it is treated as derived from it, so it has the
same licence as the driver: the GNU General Public License version 2.

hevcdec drives the Pi 4's HEVC block directly. It uses Linux's rpivid
HEVC code (rpivid_h265.c, GPL-2.0-or-later) unchanged, and fills its
controls as Raspberry Pi's FFmpeg does (LGPL-2.1-or-later). It too is
under the GNU General Public License version 2.

The licence's text is GPLv2 in this directory; the source is at the
address above.
